#: ../../source/capabilities.rst:173 1034a42ee96f450d8fe937ac85a66cf8
msgid ""
"``status()`` -- three answers rather than one number: `Fault` when the "
"code is 0 or 7 (the two a three-bit field leaves over), `State` when the "
"interval between edges stopped looking like a sector, `Ok` otherwise -- "
"plus `illegal_reads()`/`stale_reads()`, which say which channel fired. A "
"code-only decoder cannot know how wrong it is; these say whether it is "
"measuring at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/capabilities.rst:177 cade8ef8395a4b39bad6bab74123dc14
#, python-format
msgid ""
"`Param` on a non-finite timestamp; an illegal code answers a zero vector "
"and `Fault` rather than a guessed vector, and an interval that leaves "
"`[period/1.5, period*1.5]` is refused rather than adopted as the new "
"reference -- adopting it is what a dead sensor needs to stay hidden "
"(measured: 36 % of a revolution reporting `Ok` with a 120-degree error, "
