msgid "``core/watchdog.hpp``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/capabilities.rst:281 9eafa9fff22948488f73c1b0a798bc06
msgid ""
"`WatchdogState` separates the four answers a feeder can leave behind: "
"`Feeding` (inside the window), `Expired` (the window passed), `ClockLost`"
" (the stamp went backwards) and `Unarmed` (nothing measured yet). The "
"last two are the point: `Unarmed` is reported as a `State` error and "
"never as `Ok`, because a watchdog nobody feeds protects nothing, and "
"`ClockLost` is a separate state from `Expired` because the verdict is the"
" same (stop) and the diagnosis is not. A latched report repeats the "
"numbers that caused the latch instead of growing with the clock."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/capabilities.rst:286 a42f8b466d3c46618cea8b070b182d1f
